<node id="&quot;AMERICA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"America is the location of Karen Washington's activism and the origin of the term 'food apartheid'."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6c54a23f66d3bd03c066dd017416495</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE BIG LOTTERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Big Lottery is the funding source that provided a £120,000 grant to Made in Hackney, enabling its initial operations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6c54a23f66d3bd03c066dd017416495</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 241}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMACULTURE COURSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The permaculture course Sarah attended was a pivotal step in her transition from journalism to hands-on food and environmental work."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6c54a23f66d3bd03c066dd017416495</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING BID APPLICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The funding bid application written by Sarah for the health food shop led to the creation of Made in Hackney, marking the organization's origin."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6c54a23f66d3bd03c066dd017416495</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GRANT APPLICATION PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The grant application process involved extensive community consultation and was a critical factor in securing the initial funding for Made in Hackney."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b6c54a23f66d3bd03c066dd017416495</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 80}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NHS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"NHS (National Health Service) is a public health service in the UK that invited Made in Hackney to a diabetes training course, highlighting the intersection between medical advice and practical food education."&lt;SEP&gt;"NHS is the National Health Service, which receives hot cooked meals from organizations like North London Community Consortium and Blooming Scent through the Community Food Hub's support."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NHS (National Health Service) is a partner organization working with the Royal Borough to provide gardening opportunities for mental health support groups."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5576f361098cae366991f75721d79df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c3bf3a77fe43e80e44feb3007675aa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f41e016a27767cf55df9fb4111f02117</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 125}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GP SURGERIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GP surgeries are general practitioner clinics that Made in Hackney aims to affiliate with, to provide community-based cooking education as part of healthcare support."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5576f361098cae366991f75721d79df</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 241}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIABETES TRAINING COURSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Diabetes Training Course is an NHS-led event where Made in Hackney was invited to participate, highlighting the contrast between deprivation-based dietary advice and joyful, plant-based education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5576f361098cae366991f75721d79df</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 125}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUPERMARKET TOUR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Supermarket Tour is an activity conducted during the Diabetes Training Course, focusing on identifying foods to avoid rather than promoting healthy alternatives, which Made in Hackney critiqued."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5576f361098cae366991f75721d79df</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 27}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 125}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COOKING CLASSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cooking Classes are the core activities of Made in Hackney, designed to teach practical, joyful, and culturally inclusive cooking skills to improve health outcomes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e5576f361098cae366991f75721d79df</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 184}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GENERAL PRACTITIONERS (GPS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GPs are healthcare professionals who refer patients to Made in Hackney for dietary guidance, indicating a partnership between healthcare and food education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 243}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIABETES DEPARTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The diabetes department is a healthcare organization that collaborates with Made in Hackney to address dietary needs related to diabetes management."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 241}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCAL HEALTH FACILITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Local health facilities are healthcare institutions that refer patients to Made in Hackney, highlighting the integration of food education into broader healthcare services."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 241}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WEST AFRICAN PLANT-BASED FOOD PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A six-week program at Made in Hackney focused on West African plant-based cuisine, led by diverse chefs and aimed at making plant-based eating culturally accessible and appealing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 244}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NENA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Nena is a chef featured in the West African plant-based food program at Made in Hackney, recognized for her culinary expertise and role in making plant-based cuisine appealing to participants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 244}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKING POVERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Working poverty refers to a socioeconomic condition where individuals earn less than the benefit level despite being employed, highlighting systemic issues in income and cost of living."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENEFIT LEVEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Benefit level denotes the threshold of financial support provided by social welfare systems, often lagging behind rising living costs and exacerbating economic disparities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COST OF LIVING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cost of Living refers to the economic challenge that the Food Roots programme addresses by providing immediate support to food insecure Londoners."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cost of living encompasses the expenses required to maintain a standard of living, including housing, food, and utilities, which has risen disproportionately compared to wages and benefits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9f9a810e825299590c7f8d4026604afd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY ACCOMMODATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary accommodation refers to short-term housing solutions, often lacking basic amenities like kitchens, which pose barriers to healthy eating for residents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOSTEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hostel is a type of temporary accommodation where individuals may reside, often lacking the infrastructure for cooking and contributing to barriers in accessing healthy food."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SHELTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Shelter refers to emergency or transitional housing provided to individuals in need, often lacking kitchens and exacerbating challenges in maintaining a healthy diet."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 186}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CULTURAL CONNECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cultural connection refers to the link between food and heritage, emphasizing the importance of preserving traditional culinary practices in promoting plant-based eating."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL ACTIVISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental activism involves efforts to promote sustainability and reduce ecological impact, often intersecting with food choices and dietary education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INDUSTRIALIZED MEAT FARMING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Industrialized meat farming refers to large-scale livestock production systems, often criticized for their environmental and ethical impacts, which are discussed in the context of promoting plant-based diets."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COLLABORATIVE LEARNING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Collaborative learning is an educational approach that emphasizes mutual exchange and shared knowledge, contrasting with traditional teacher-student dynamics in food education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POWER DYNAMICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Power dynamics refer to the relationships of power and influence between individuals or groups, often evident in healthcare settings where doctors and patients have unequal roles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CULTURAL FOOD NEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cultural food needs encompass the dietary preferences, traditions, and restrictions tied to a person's cultural background, which must be respected in food education programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD ACTIVISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Food activism involves advocating for changes in food systems, policies, and practices to promote health, sustainability, and social justice."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL JUSTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental justice focuses on the fair treatment and meaningful involvement of all people in environmental decision-making, particularly affecting marginalized communities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH INEQUITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Health inequities refer to avoidable differences in health status among populations, often linked to socioeconomic factors and systemic barriers to accessing nutritious food."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 190}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC DISPARITIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Economic disparities refer to the unequal distribution of wealth and resources, which can impact access to healthy food and contribute to systemic health and social challenges."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL WELFARE SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social welfare systems are institutional frameworks designed to provide support to individuals in need, including financial assistance and housing, which are critical in addressing poverty and inequality."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CAPITALISM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Capitalism is an economic system characterized by private ownership of production and the pursuit of profit, which can influence wage structures and access to resources in ways that exacerbate social and economic inequalities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 185}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSTAINABLE FOOD SYSTEMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sustainable food systems aim to balance environmental, economic, and social needs, ensuring that food production and consumption are ecologically responsible and socially equitable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 23}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 212}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD EDUCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Food Education is an implicit aspect of FoodCycle's mission, promoting awareness of healthy eating and food waste reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food education involves teaching individuals about nutrition, cooking, and healthy eating habits, often tailored to address cultural, economic, and environmental factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b93322b0388501e0ea84654d7f52bdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTHCARE PARTNERSHIPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Healthcare partnerships involve collaborations between health professionals and community organizations to improve patient outcomes through integrated services and education."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 243}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD SOVEREIGNTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Advocacy efforts by Transition groups to empower communities to control their own food systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food sovereignty is the right of communities to define their own food systems, prioritizing local knowledge, traditions, and ecological sustainability over corporate interests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-444de3c543eba40970e27cff27051d4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 75}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC INEQUALITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Systemic inequality refers to the entrenched, institutionalized disparities in access to resources, opportunities, and services that disproportionately affect marginalized groups."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 190}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECONOMIC EMPOWERMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Economic empowerment involves enabling individuals and communities to gain control over their economic resources and improve their quality of life through education, employment, and financial inclusion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOCIAL COHESION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Social Cohesion is linked to the benefits of tended gardens, as neighborhoods with active gardening see reduced crime and stronger community bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social cohesion refers to the bonds that unite members of a society, fostering trust, cooperation, and a shared sense of identity and purpose."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d82cdcdea65463aa40e9d63536c0cca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 242}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH LITERACY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Health literacy involves the ability to obtain, process, and understand basic health information and services to make informed health decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL AWARENESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental awareness involves understanding the impact of individual and collective actions on the environment, often driving sustainable behaviors and policy changes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 241}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CULTURAL COMPETENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cultural competence refers to the ability to understand, communicate with, and effectively interact with people across cultures, which is essential in food education and healthcare settings."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 182}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH EQUITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Health equity refers to the principle that everyone should have the opportunity to attain their full health potential, without discrimination based on socioeconomic status, race, or other factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 190}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUSTAINABLE LIVELIHOODS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sustainable livelihoods involve meeting basic needs while maintaining or enhancing the natural resource base, ensuring long-term economic and environmental stability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 187}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOOD JUSTICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Efforts by Transition groups to ensure equitable access to food and challenge systemic barriers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food justice is a concept discussed as essential for addressing systemic inequalities and ensuring equitable access to food and resources for marginalized communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food justice is a movement that seeks to address the root causes of food insecurity and inequity, advocating for policies and practices that ensure fair access to nutritious food for all."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-444de3c543eba40970e27cff27051d4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbdcee9e5e42f35143c82e778ee4d879&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 36}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY RESILIENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community resilience refers to the ability of communities to withstand, adapt to, and recover from challenges, often strengthened through collective action and resource-sharing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 181}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 242}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL STEWARDSHIP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Environmental Stewardship is a key component of the Farm's training programs, teaching volunteers about caring for the environment and promoting eco-diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental stewardship involves the responsible management and protection of natural resources, often driven by individuals and organizations committed to sustainability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-94a6abfb598dc0466e023c4920e30adf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 83}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEALTH PROMOTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Health promotion involves creating conditions that support healthy behaviors and lifestyles, often through education, policy changes, and community initiatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4977d07d758202d37b9bcafe187cf775</data>
