<node id="&quot;WESTMINSTER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">Here is a comprehensive summary of the data provided:

Westminster is a borough in London, United Kingdom, that holds significant historical and political importance. It is the seat of the UK government and has been historically and politically significant since its inception. The borough is also home to various community organizations and initiatives, including CommunityFridgeMap, Lend and Tend, and the Trussell Trust.

Westminster is a hub for food-related activities, with several community gardens and initiatives located within the district. These include the West Hampstead Community Food Hub, which is based at the Sidings Community Centre, and the CSA Network UK, which has its coordinates listed as 51.5074, -0.1278.

The borough is also associated with various organizations and projects, including Made in Hackney, Milly Giveaway, and Xcess. Additionally, Westminster is home to several notable landmarks, such as the Houses of Parliament and Westminster Abbey, which are significant to its political and historical importance.

Despite some variations in description, all sources agree that Westminster is a borough within London, United Kingdom, with specific coordinates listed for various locations. The district is also mentioned as being part of the Royal Borough of Kensington and Chelsea, although this may be an error given the context.

Overall, Westminster is a unique and significant borough in London, known for its historical and political importance, as well as its role in community food-related initiatives and activities.</data>
