<node id="&quot;UNITED KINGDOM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">The United Kingdom is a sovereign country located off the north-western coast of mainland Europe, encompassing England, Scotland, Wales, and Northern Ireland. It is a country where various organizations operate, including Edible Landscapes London, Food Bank Aid, Good to Grow, Hornsey Food Bank, Islington, London, Made In Hackney, Milly Giveaway, OmVed Gardens, Plan Zheroes, Spitalfields City Farm, Sutton Community Farm, The Village Centre, UKHarvest, Vauxhall City Farm, Xcess, Fareshares Food Co-op, Infinity Foods, Chelsea Physic Garden, Connected Seeds Library, Heritage Seed Library, Lend and Tend, Limborough Food Hub, London Freedom Seed Bank, Royal Borough of Kensington and Chelsea, West Hampstead Community Food Hub, Extinction Rebellion, Cultivate London, Neighbourly, Coronation Food Project, UK CSA Network, and many others. The country is also home to various community gardens, including the one located in London, as well as community kitchens such as the London and Bermondsey Community Kitchen, which operates specifically in the London borough of Southwark.

The United Kingdom is a country where food poverty and hunger are significant issues, with organizations like Trussell Trust operating to address these problems. The country is also home to various initiatives aimed at promoting sustainable food systems, such as the Sustainable Food Places initiative and the Community Supported Agriculture (CSA) Network UK.

In addition, the United Kingdom is a country where community-led initiatives, such as the Community Dinners and the Soup Kitchen, operate to provide food assistance to those in need. The country is also home to various organizations that promote urban agriculture and climate action, including Extinction Rebellion and Cultivate London.

The United Kingdom is a country with diverse landscapes, historical sites, and cultural heritage, known for its capital city, London, which is located in the northwest of Europe.</data>
